From: Balazs Gyimesi <gyimesi.balazs@gmail.com>
Subject: spi: qpic-snand: allow skipping the SPI config init on TZ-locked controllers

On secure-boot IPQ5018 units (Xiaomi CB0401V2) TrustZone XPU-protects the
SPI-NAND mode registers (NAND_FLASH_SPI_CFG, NAND_NUM_ADDR_CYCLES,
NAND_BUSY_CHECK_WAIT_CNT): any access from the HLOS is a secure violation
that halts the SoC. TZ has already programmed them for the boot chain, so
with the "qcom,tz-locked-spi-cfg" DT property the driver skips its own
init and uses the configuration left by the firmware.

--- a/drivers/spi/spi-qpic-snand.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-qpic-snand.c
@@ -1593,7 +1593,17 @@
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_snand_alloc;
 
-	ret = qcom_spi_init(snandc);
+	/*
+	 * Secure-boot units may have the SPI config registers locked by
+	 * TrustZone (XPU); touching them halts the system. TZ has set them up
+	 * for the boot chain already, so keep its configuration.
+	 */
+	if (of_property_read_bool(dev->of_node, "qcom,tz-locked-spi-cfg")) {
+		dev_info(dev, "SPI config registers are TZ-locked, skipping init\n");
+		ret = 0;
+	} else {
+		ret = qcom_spi_init(snandc);
+	}
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_spi_init;
 
